(5019793, 732889, 15407, '<td valign="top">Indeed... The High Rent District!  The colors and compodurelook great!</td>', 'Indeed... The High Rent District!  The colors and compodurelook great!', '2008-10-22 04:08:31.000000', NULL, 1),
(5019814, 732834, 96881, '<td valign="top">Exceptional capture.  The sharpness of this photo and the reflections make this a stand out.  Would also love to see the colour version.  Only (very minor) thing would be the background (ideally, which is usually impossible) would have been great if it was either darker or lighter than it is.  Its too close to the car at the moment.<br/>But hey, that is only the most minor of things.<br/>Excellent Job.....Well Done on a Great Photo</td>', 'Exceptional capture.  The sharpness of this photo and the reflections make this a stand out.  Would also love to see the colour version.  Only (very minor) thing would be the background (ideally, which is usually impossible) would have been great if it was either darker or lighter than it is.  Its too close to the car at the moment.But hey, that is only the most minor of things.Excellent Job.....Well Done on a Great Photo', '2008-10-22 04:15:11.000000', NULL, 1),
(5019817, 732880, 96881, '<td valign="top">A classic take on the topic.<br/>The exceptionally narrow depth of field, while well done technically, does not work for me here.  It makes the photo a little too much OOF for my liking, and also the overall photo too dark as well as a result</td>', 'A classic take on the topic.The exceptionally narrow depth of field, while well done technically, does not work for me here.  It makes the photo a little too much OOF for my liking, and also the overall photo too dark as well as a result', '2008-10-22 04:16:57.000000', NULL, 1),
(5019820, 732484, 96881, '<td valign="top">It does seem safer.<br/>Great Idea and great execution.  Light from the candles to help light the box is great.  I would have been tempted to be slightly fdurther out, and make more use of the reflections as well (would need to see the result though) as at the moment the candle reflections (especially the small one) are awkwardly cropped (can just see the light glow from it)<br/>But thats minor.  Great capture here.  Well Done</td>', 'It does seem safer.Great Idea and great execution.  Light from the candles to help light the box is great.  I would have been tempted to be slightly fdurther out, and make more use of the reflections as well (would need to see the result though) as at the moment the candle reflections (especially the small one) are awkwardly cropped (can just see the light glow from it)But thats minor.  Great capture here.  Well Done', '2008-10-22 04:20:01.000000', NULL, 1),
(5019823, 732200, 15407, '<td valign="top">Gotta love the Fog... Sometimes it adds a great effect there &amp; others it makes it very tough. The neighborhood &amp; views are indeed Affluent.</td>', 'Gotta love the Fog... Sometimes it adds a great effect there & others it makes it very tough. The neighborhood & views are indeed Affluent.', '2008-10-22 04:21:58.000000', NULL, 1),
(5019824, 732713, 96881, '<td valign="top">The depth of field is a little too narrow for me.  The letters are not all sharp (especially H, U and R).  I would have preferred to see this as a very sharp capture of the traditional grill and HUMMER.<br/>The crop works. The idea was good, the angle of view ios also good though</td>', 'The depth of field is a little too narrow for me.  The letters are not all sharp (especially H, U and R).  I would have preferred to see this as a very sharp capture of the traditional grill and HUMMER.The crop works. The idea was good, the angle of view ios also good though', '2008-10-22 04:21:59.000000', NULL, 1),
(5019828, 732849, 96881, '<td valign="top">I see this as a family snapshot, best suited to the Family Album.  The photo in no way represents the topic for me.<br/>Sorry..........</td>', 'I see this as a family snapshot, best suited to the Family Album.  The photo in no way represents the topic for me.Sorry..........', '2008-10-22 04:25:55.000000', NULL, 1),
(5019829, 732829, 96881, '<td valign="top">Like the idea, the curving nests work (much better than if they were straight).  Depth of field is really good.  I like the lighting of it as well.  I probably would have had the front nest though all in the picture, instead of cropping off the right hand notes, but would still of had the egg to the right hand side of the photo.  A little bit more room both the left and right side for me.<br/>But thats all minor.  Great idea and good execution.  Well Done!</td>', 'Like the idea, the curving nests work (much better than if they were straight).  Depth of field is really good.  I like the lighting of it as well.  I probably would have had the front nest though all in the picture, instead of cropping off the right hand notes, but would still of had the egg to the right hand side of the photo.  A little bit more room both the left and right side for me.But thats all minor.  Great idea and good execution.  Well Done!', '2008-10-22 04:28:59.000000', NULL, 1),
(5019831, 731888, 96881, '<td valign="top">Not really sure how this meets the challenge, but ignoring that.......<br/>A narrower depth of field would have blurred the crowd more, and those standing ont eh touchline.  As a result, it would have made the players stand out more, rather than blending intot he background a little.<br/>The title doesn''t seem to match the photo.  Doesn''t show a lot of joy.  Shows soemone about to lay a tackle (or miss the tackle)...</td>', 'Not really sure how this meets the challenge, but ignoring that.......A narrower depth of field would have blurred the crowd more, and those standing ont eh touchline.  As a result, it would have made the players stand out more, rather than blending intot he background a little.The title doesn''t seem to match the photo.  Doesn''t show a lot of joy.  Shows soemone about to lay a tackle (or miss the tackle)...', '2008-10-22 04:32:36.000000', NULL, 1),
(5019837, 732701, 96881, '<td valign="top">To me, the numberplate , as a result of the lighting, colour and crop is the dominent focus of the photo, rather than the Mercedes Badge or the Car in general.  This detracts from the photo and the message. I dopn''t think the tight crop works here.  This photo needed more of the bonnet, and the tight crop on the sides does not work.  Panoramic Crops also have a history of not scoring well here.  The lighting though is the big thing.  Better lighting is needed to get the eyes to notice the car, or the badge, instead of the number plate, as the main theme.</td>', 'To me, the numberplate , as a result of the lighting, colour and crop is the dominent focus of the photo, rather than the Mercedes Badge or the Car in general.  This detracts from the photo and the message. I dopn''t think the tight crop works here.  This photo needed more of the bonnet, and the tight crop on the sides does not work.  Panoramic Crops also have a history of not scoring well here.  The lighting though is the big thing.  Better lighting is needed to get the eyes to notice the car, or the badge, instead of the number plate, as the main theme.', '2008-10-22 04:59:37.000000', NULL, 1),
(5019840, 732882, 96881, '<td valign="top">Not a fan of the lighting in this photo.  The overall photo is not interesting.  The lack of a title means we are unable to see where you are coming from with this.  The White/Black changhe in the photo does not work</td>', 'Not a fan of the lighting in this photo.  The overall photo is not interesting.  The lack of a title means we are unable to see where you are coming from with this.  The White/Black changhe in the photo does not work', '2008-10-22 05:01:22.000000', NULL, 1),
(5019842, 732882, 90197, '<td valign="top">???</td>', '???', '2008-10-22 05:02:59.000000', NULL, 1),
(5019844, 731433, 96881, '<td valign="top">The angle of the photo does not work for me.  I would prefer a higher view where we were looking up the bonnet as well, or instead a different angle that shows the lines of the car, both its bonnet and the sides.  The lighting also does not flatter the car.</td>', 'The angle of the photo does not work for me.  I would prefer a higher view where we were looking up the bonnet as well, or instead a different angle that shows the lines of the car, both its bonnet and the sides.  The lighting also does not flatter the car.', '2008-10-22 05:03:32.000000', NULL, 1),
