(5042296, 732890, 68947, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by yospiff:</b></div><hr/><i> It does not stink at all. It is on the higher side of a 5 and I can see in the voting breakdown that a lot of people liked it. You just had a large batch of 4''s dragging it down as well. I think this may have just needed a little more visual impact in it. Maybe some slightly different lighting of a touch of some additional adjustment? Not really sure. I gave it a 5. </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>LOL Steve...."it doesn''t stink at all"!  Thank you for your kind words here.  I agree that it needed something else, but everything in there was FAKE...including the fur that everything rested upon...as one can tell, obviously.  I do agree with you on your points.  I''ll keep those in mind.</td>', 'Originally posted by yospiff: It does not stink at all. It is on the higher side of a 5 and I can see in the voting breakdown that a lot of people liked it. You just had a large batch of 4''s dragging it down as well. I think this may have just needed a little more visual impact in it. Maybe some slightly different lighting of a touch of some additional adjustment? Not really sure. I gave it a 5.   LOL Steve...."it doesn''t stink at all"!  Thank you for your kind words here.  I agree that it needed something else, but everything in there was FAKE...including the fur that everything rested upon...as one can tell, obviously.  I do agree with you on your points.  I''ll keep those in mind.', '2008-11-03 20:19:35.000000', NULL, 0),
(5042937, 732755, 67258, '<td valign="top">Hello from the Critique Club, here are my thoughts on your photo:<br/> <br/>Initial thoughts - a good take on the challenge theme with an amusing and very appropriate title thta compliments the photo. <br/> <br/>Technicals - exposure was always going to be a hard one to nail, with the large tonal range.  I would say that you have very marginally over-exposed:  there is some detail in the dog''s coat, but the overall brightness of the white makes the detail hard to pick out.  The composition is right, given the constraints of candid photography; the diagonal of the path, echoed by the diagonal of the lead is pleasing, although the placement of some elements of the background, notably the bush in the left of frame is, for me at least, less beneficial to the shot.  Did you explore any other crops?  I masked off below the second row of windows, and found a crop that I felt had more impact, but as with all things compositional, it comes down to subjective aesthetics and opinion.  I do find the slight tilt to the right somewhat uncomfortable, although it may be that it gives a greater sense of presence to the woman.<br/> <br/>Overall impression - an interesting commentary on a clearly affluent and fashion-conscious lifestyle that is a subtle but very valid take on the challenge.<br/> <br/>If you have any queries, do send me a PM.</td>', 'Hello from the Critique Club, here are my thoughts on your photo: Initial thoughts - a good take on the challenge theme with an amusing and very appropriate title thta compliments the photo.  Technicals - exposure was always going to be a hard one to nail, with the large tonal range.  I would say that you have very marginally over-exposed:  there is some detail in the dog''s coat, but the overall brightness of the white makes the detail hard to pick out.  The composition is right, given the constraints of candid photography; the diagonal of the path, echoed by the diagonal of the lead is pleasing, although the placement of some elements of the background, notably the bush in the left of frame is, for me at least, less beneficial to the shot.  Did you explore any other crops?  I masked off below the second row of windows, and found a crop that I felt had more impact, but as with all things compositional, it comes down to subjective aesthetics and opinion.  I do find the slight tilt to the right somewhat uncomfortable, although it may be that it gives a greater sense of presence to the woman. Overall impression - an interesting commentary on a clearly affluent and fashion-conscious lifestyle that is a subtle but very valid take on the challenge. If you have any queries, do send me a PM.', '2008-11-04 08:18:45.000000', NULL, 0),
(5047404, 732788, 83313, '<td valign="top">Great idea! Sorry I missed it in voting. I like your location description as well.<br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2008-11-05 18:54:26.</i></td>', 'Great idea! Sorry I missed it in voting. I like your location description as well.', '2008-11-05 18:53:30.000000', '2008-11-05 18:54:26.000000', 0),
(5054271, 732788, 61651, '<td valign="top">I always enjoy seeing your entries in these challenges, Susan - you often put so much effort and thought into the set up.  Another funny take here, and I can appreciate your difficulties with minimizing those shadows - no you didn''t beat them, but you put in a valiant effort.  I wish I could give you a tip here to help for the future, but the issue has me a bit stumped too. :)</td>', 'I always enjoy seeing your entries in these challenges, Susan - you often put so much effort and thought into the set up.  Another funny take here, and I can appreciate your difficulties with minimizing those shadows - no you didn''t beat them, but you put in a valiant effort.  I wish I could give you a tip here to help for the future, but the issue has me a bit stumped too. :)', '2008-11-09 23:13:19.000000', NULL, 0),
